BT 1 0 0 1 0 46.4 Tm 14 TL /F1 9.6 Tf .105882 .121569 .164706 rg (Three things stand out in the script: a large integer array ) Tj /F3 9.6 Tf (_0xcfg) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf (, a small function that XORs each element with a key,) Tj T* -0.0656 Tw (and the line ) Tj /F3 9.6 Tf (var _k = \(0x30 ^ 0x0b\)) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf (. The key is written as an expression so a quick glance does not reveal it, but) Tj T* 0 Tw (it evaluates to ) Tj /F3 9.6 Tf (0x3b) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf (. The checksum function ) Tj /F3 9.6 Tf (_0x9f) Tj /F1 9.6 Tf ( does nothing useful; it is a decoy. The lab build also stripped the) Tj T* (download-and-execute calls, so decoding the array is all that is needed.) Tj T* ET
