BT 1 0 0 1 0 46.4 Tm /F1 9.6 Tf 14 TL (That repeated prefix is the clue. Two messages with the same first bytes can only come from the same plaintext start) Tj T* (encrypted with the same keystream start. So the cipher is restarted for each message \(a fresh RC4 per packet\), and) Tj T* (the commands share a common beginning. A single running keystream would make every packet look different. So:) Tj T* (decrypt each payload independently, with no header to skip.) Tj T* ET
